  "note": "Sys.g not given: EasySpin uses gfree = 2.00231930436092. Scalar lwpp = Gaussian. garlic (no fast motion) builds the spectrum with Opt.AccumMethod='binning': makespec(...,'round') snaps each line to the NEAREST grid point, then convolves with a sampled lineshape. An analytic-line simulator cannot reproduce the snapping, so the reference itself carries a grid error. Measured: analytic Gaussian + exact modulation integral differs by 4.4e-3 of max; with the line snapped to the nearest grid point (346.1222 instead of 346.1201 mT) it reproduces the reference to 5e-12, which also confirms g = gfree, Gaussian lwpp and peak-to-peak ModAmp.",
